{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1127222-love-among-the-fera","id":1127222,"title":"Love among the Fera","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-10T11:49:51-07:00","id":1127222,"title":"Love among the Fera","content":"While the majority of the Fera are literally combat monsters, reproduction is an essential duty of all of the Fera (as they are required to produce Kinfolk and Fera children). In the case of Homid Fera, their duty to reproduction could also be considered to be a duty to love, as human beings often associate reproduction with love (love of the children and, possibly, love of the reproductive partner). How do you handle love in your games when one of the partners are Fera?<br /> <br /> In my games, there are significant differences between male and female Fera when it comes to the practice of love. Male Fera are encouraged to spread their seed among the unmarried female Kinfolk, so to speak, in order to maximize the chance of getting the female Kinfolk pregnant (unmarried female Kinfolk get to select the male Fera that will sleep with them and, if they get pregnant, they get their choice in unmarried male Kinfolk to marry). Female Fera are encouraged to get married to male Kinfolk, though the Fera normally do not care if their husband is the father of their children, the Fera just want someone to take care of the children when the female Fera is off doing her duties. In my game, love is often a dream for male Fera while it is a reality for female Fera (Metis are uncommon in my games, as they are one percent of the Fera population, and no one cares who they fall in love with as long as they do not block the reproduction of Fera or Kinfolk). In the case of homosexual Fera or Kinfolk, as long as it does not interfere with reproduction, no one really cares who Fera or Kinfolk love. What about your games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T13:52:28-07:00","id":1127304,"title":"","content":"I&quot;m not as heavily biased towards the nuclear family as the end all, be all of sexual dynamics. I imagine that in the more social breeds its very much &quot;the Sept/Court&quot; takes care of the kids, they have alot of aunts and uncles who show up and watch over them(fellow members of the sentai/pack, Den parents). While there are lost kinfolk and cubs I imagine the majority are raised by a variety of people because Fera lives are profoundly violent.<br /> <br /> How the more solitary &quot;We have no real organization&quot; types like most Bastet seem to work out I have no idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}